codex
The torus action gives a safe global normalization: every point with \(c\ne0\) can be moved to \(c=1\). That removes both \(c\) and its inverse variable from the solver ring. The bigrading also shows that a certificate for \(c^N\) can use only Jacobian rows with \(x\)-index at most \(N(\ell+1)-1\); this restricts certificate search without specializing any chart parameters.

